{"id":"mahabharata-6-087","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":87,"title":"सप्ताशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 87 · Ghatotkacha's rage","summary":{"en":"On seeing Iravan dead, Ghatotkacha roars and attacks the Kaurava army with his demon troops. He rushes at Duryodhana, who stands against his showers of arrows.","kn":"ಇರಾವಾನನ ಸಾವು ಕಂಡು ಘಟೋತ್ಕಚ ಗರ್ಜಿಸಿ ರಾಕ್ಷಸ ಸೈನ್ಯದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯದ ಮೇಲೆ ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಬಾಣಮಳೆಯನ್ನು ಎದುರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"इरावान् की मृत्यु देखकर घटोत्कच गरजकर राक्षस-सेना सहित कौरव सेना पर टूट पड़ता है। वह दुर्योधन पर झपटता है, जो उसकी बाण-वर्षा का सामना करता है।","te":"ఇరావంతుని మరణం చూసి ఘటోత్కచుడు గర్జించి రాక్షససేనతో కౌరవసేనపై పడతాడు. దుర్యోధనునిపైకి దూసుకెళతాడు; దుర్యోధనుడు అతని బాణవర్షాన్ని ఎదుర్కొంటాడు.","ta":"இராவானின் மரணத்தைக் கண்ட கடோத்கசன் முழங்கி அரக்கப் படையுடன் கௌரவப் படையைத் தாக்குகிறான். துரியோதனனை நோக்கிப் பாய, அவன் அம்பு மழையை எதிர்கொள்கிறான்.","ml":"ഇരാവൻ മരിച്ചുകിടക്കുന്നത് കണ്ട ഘടോൽക്കചൻ അലറി രാക്ഷസ സേനയോടുകൂടി കൗരവ സൈന്യത്തെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു. അമ്പുമഴ ചൊരിയുന്ന അദ്ദേഹത്തെ നേരിടാൻ നിൽക്കുന്ന ദുര്യോധനന്റെ നേരെ അദ്ദേഹം പാഞ്ഞടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.87; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"इरावन्तं तु निहतं दृष्ट्वा पार्था महारथाः ।\nसंग्रामे किमकुर्वन्त तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the great chariot-warrior sons of Pritha saw Iravan killed, what did they do in the battle? Tell me that, Sanjaya."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"इरावन्तं तु निहतं संग्रामे वीक्ष्य राक्षसः ।\nव्यनदत्सुमहानादं भैमसेनिर्घटोत्कचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Iravan killed in the battle, the rakshasa Ghatotkacha, son of Bhima, let out a very loud roar."}},{"n":3,"text":"नदतस्तस्य शब्देन पृथिवी सागराम्बरा ।\nसपर्वतवना राजंश्चचाल सुभृशं तदा ।\nअन्तरिक्षं दिशश्चैव सर्वाश्च प्रदिशस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the sound of his roaring the earth with its oceans and sky, its mountains and forests, shook greatly, O king, and so did the sky, the directions and all the intermediate quarters."}},{"n":4,"text":"तं श्रुत्वा सुमहानादं तव सैन्यस्य भारत ।\nऊरुस्तम्भः समभवद्वेपथुः स्वेद एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that great roar, O Bharata, your army was seized with stiffness in the thighs, trembling and sweat."}},{"n":5,"text":"सर्व एव च राजेन्द्र तावका दीनचेतसः ।\nसर्पवत्समवेष्टन्त सिंहभीता गजा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"All your men, O king of kings, were dejected in mind; they writhed like snakes, like elephants afraid of a lion."}},{"n":6,"text":"निनदत्सुमहानादं निर्घातमिव राक्षसः ।\nज्वलितं शूलमुद्यम्य रूपं कृत्वा विभीषणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rakshasa, roaring a great roar like a thunderclap, took up a blazing spear and assumed a frightful form."}},{"n":7,"text":"नानाप्रहरणैर्घोरैर्वृतो राक्षसपुंगवैः ।\nआजगाम सुसंक्रुद्धः कालान्तकयमोपमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by the foremost of rakshasas with terrible weapons of many kinds, he came on in great rage, like Time, the Ender, and Yama."}},{"n":8,"text":"तमापतन्तं संप्रेक्ष्य संक्रुद्धं भीमदर्शनम् ।\nस्वबलं च भयात्तस्य प्रायशो विमुखीकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him coming, enraged and fearful to look at, Duryodhana's own army, from fear of him, was mostly turned away."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा घटोत्कचमुपाद्रवत् ।\nप्रगृह्य विपुलं चापं सिंहवद्विनदन्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, taking up a huge bow and roaring again and again like a lion, ran at Ghatotkacha."}},{"n":10,"text":"पृष्ठतोऽनुययौ चैनं स्रवद्भिः पर्वतोपमैः ।\nकुञ्जरैर्दशसाहस्रैर्वङ्गानामधिपः स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of the Vangas himself followed behind him with ten thousand elephants like mountains, their temples streaming."}},{"n":11,"text":"तमापतन्तं संप्रेक्ष्य गजानीकेन संवृतम् ।\nपुत्रं तव महाराज चुकोप स निशाचरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your son coming, O great king, surrounded by the elephant division, the night-roamer was enraged."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततः प्रववृते युद्धं तुमुलं लोमहर्षणम् ।\nराक्षसानां च राजेन्द्र दुर्योधनबलस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a tumultuous, hair-raising battle began between the rakshasas and Duryodhana's force, O king of kings."}},{"n":13,"text":"गजानीकं च संप्रेक्ष्य मेघवृन्दमिवोद्यतम् ।\nअभ्यधावन्त संक्रुद्धा राक्षसाः शस्त्रपाणयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the elephant division risen like a mass of clouds, the enraged rakshasas, weapons in hand, ran at it."}},{"n":14,"text":"नदन्तो विविधान्नादान्मेघा इव सविद्युतः ।\nशरशक्त्यृष्टिनाराचैर्निघ्नन्तो गजयोधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Roaring in many ways like clouds with lightning, they killed the elephant-fighters with arrows, spears, lances and iron arrows."}},{"n":15,"text":"भिण्डिपालैस्तथा शूलैर्मुद्गरैः सपरश्वधैः ।\nपर्वताग्रैश्च वृक्षैश्च निजघ्नुस्ते महागजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With barbed darts, javelins, clubs and axes, and with mountain peaks and trees, they struck down the great elephants."}},{"n":16,"text":"भिन्नकुम्भान्विरुधिरान्भिन्नगात्रांश्च वारणान् ।\nअपश्याम महाराज वध्यमानान्निशाचरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, we saw the elephants with split foreheads and bodies, bleeding, being killed by the night-roamers."}},{"n":17,"text":"तेषु प्रक्षीयमाणेषु भग्नेषु गजयोधिषु ।\nदुर्योधनो महाराज राक्षसान्समुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the elephant-fighters were being destroyed and broken, O great king, Duryodhana charged at the rakshasas."}},{"n":18,"text":"अमर्षवशमापन्नस्त्यक्त्वा जीवितमात्मनः ।\nमुमोच निशितान्बाणान्राक्षसेषु महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Overcome with fury and careless of his own life, the mighty king loosed sharp arrows at the rakshasas."}},{"n":19,"text":"जघान च महेष्वासः प्रधानांस्तत्र राक्षसान् ।\nसंक्रुद्धो भरतश्रेष्ठ पुत्रो दुर्योधनस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great bowman, your son Duryodhana, best of Bharatas, enraged, killed the chief rakshasas there."}},{"n":20,"text":"वेगवन्तं महारौद्रं विद्युज्जिह्वं प्रमाथिनम् ।\nशरैश्चतुर्भिश्चतुरो निजघान महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great chariot-warrior killed with four arrows the four named Vegavat, Mahaarudra, Vidyujjihva and Pramathin."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः पुनरमेयात्मा शरवर्षं दुरासदम् ।\nमुमोच भरतश्रेष्ठ निशाचरबलं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O best of Bharatas, that man of boundless spirit loosed a hard-to-bear shower of arrows at the rakshasa force."}},{"n":22,"text":"तत्तु दृष्ट्वा महत्कर्म पुत्रस्य तव मारिष ।\nक्रोधेनाभिप्रजज्वाल भैमसेनिर्महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that great deed of your son, O revered one, mighty Ghatotkacha, son of Bhima, blazed up with anger."}},{"n":23,"text":"विस्फार्य च महच्चापमिन्द्राशनिसमस्वनम् ।\nअभिदुद्राव वेगेन दुर्योधनमरिंदमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stretching his great bow, whose sound was like Indra's thunderbolt, he rushed with speed at Duryodhana, the tormentor of foes."}},{"n":24,"text":"तमापतन्तमुद्वीक्ष्य कालसृष्टमिवान्तकम् ।\nन विव्यथे महाराज पुत्रो दुर्योधनस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him coming like Death sent by Time, your son Duryodhana, O great king, did not tremble."}},{"n":25,"text":"अथैनमब्रवीत्क्रुद्धः क्रूरः संरक्तलोचनः ।\nये त्वया सुनृशंसेन दीर्घकालं प्रवासिताः ।\nयच्च ते पाण्डवा राजंश्छलद्यूते पराजिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he, cruel, with red eyes, said angrily to him: You, most cruel one, drove the Pandavas away for a long time, and, O king, you beat them at the rigged dice game."}},{"n":26,"text":"यच्चैव द्रौपदी कृष्णा एकवस्त्रा रजस्वला ।\nसभामानीय दुर्बुद्धे बहुधा क्लेशिता त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Draupadi Krishna, in a single cloth and in her monthly course, you, foolish one, brought to the assembly hall and tormented in many ways."}},{"n":27,"text":"तव च प्रियकामेन आश्रमस्था दुरात्मना ।\nसैन्धवेन परिक्लिष्टा परिभूय पितॄन्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"And to please you, that wicked Saindhava tormented her as she stayed in the hermitage, insulting my fathers."}},{"n":28,"text":"एतेषामवमानानामन्येषां च कुलाधम ।\nअन्तमद्य गमिष्यामि यदि नोत्सृजसे रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For these insults and others, O lowest of your family, I will reach their end today, if you do not leave the battle."}},{"n":29,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा तु हैडिम्बो महद्विस्फार्य कार्मुकम् ।\nसंदश्य दशनैरोष्ठं सृक्किणी परिसंलिहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, Hidimba's son stretched his great bow, biting his lip with his teeth and licking the corners of his mouth."}},{"n":30,"text":"शरवर्षेण महता दुर्योधनमवाकिरत् ।\nपर्वतं वारिधाराभिः प्रावृषीव बलाहकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He covered Duryodhana with a great shower of arrows, as a cloud in the rainy season covers a mountain with streams of water."}}]}]}